- Weapon Pattern & Projectile Behaviours (gameplay/weapons.js or gameplay/projectiles.js) [DONE]
-- Right now bullets only travel in straight lines. Swarm games need archetype patterns:
-- Spread / Burst Cones (shotguns, multi-barrel barrages)
-- Orbiting Blades / Shields (persistent hitboxes rotating around the player with per-enemy hit cooldowns)
-- Chain / Ricochet (queries SpatialHash on hit to bounce to the nearest unhit enemy within range)
-- Boomerang / Homing (projectiles that decelerate and return to the player, or steer toward targets)
-- Ground Hazard Zones (lingering fire/acid pools ticking via SpatialHash.queryRadius).

- Swarm Director & Surround Slot Coordinator (ai/director.js)
-- Intensity Pacing: Instead of static wave timers, a director monitors active enemy count and player HP/DPS to alternate between high-pressure swarm surges, elite/miniboss spawns, and brief loot-collection breathers.
-- Surround Slots: Assigns angular ring slots around the player so 50 melee enemies naturally encircle the player from all sides instead of conga-lining along the exact same FlowField lane.

- Offscreen Tilemap Chunk Renderer (world/tilemapRenderer.js or inside Tilemap)
-- Drawing hundreds of individual floor and wall tiles with ctx.fillRect every frame costs CPU canvas state calls. Pre-rendering static Tilemap layers onto an offscreen <canvas> once when loadGrid() runs allows render() to draw the entire map in a single ctx.drawImage() call.

